nded, high-profile challenger with national GOP backing"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to an eight-point Democratic edge, combining Cuellar's incumbency advantage and a favorable national environment against the district's Republican lean, and markets price his win odds near 90%. The one recent poll shows Cuellar up eleven, though polling is thin, so uncertainty stays elevated.", "watch": "A late surge from Tijerina's well-funded campaign or further erosion of Cuellar's standing with South Texas Latino voters could tighten the race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Henry Cuellar (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Henry Cuellar, one of the House's most conservative Democrats, seeks another term in a South Texas district that leans Republican by three points but that he has held for two decades. He faces Tano Tijerina, a Laredo-area county judge and recent party convert who has run a visible, well-funded campaign with national Republican attention, attacking Cuellar over ethics issues. A Green Party candidate is also on the ballot.\n\nFundamentals still favor Cuellar: incumbency, a strong Democratic midterm environment, and a modest cash edge, with an August poll showing him ahead by eleven. Markets and most raters see him as likely to win, though several rate the race only Lean D given the district's lean and Tijerina's profile. The forecast expects Cuellar to prevail by roughly eight points, with meaningful uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9009, "margin": 7.69}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8765, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8779, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8804, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8627, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8617, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8973, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8968, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9013, "margin": 8.0}]}